mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# BillPay Backend API\n\nBackend for a wallet-based bill payment and mobile data reselling app. Users\nsign in with Internet Identity, hold a personal wallet balance, buy mobile data\nbundles, and pay bills. Every wallet movement is recorded in a ledger and\nmirrored into a unified transaction history.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n  `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding\n  the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app\n  principal against that origin (for example\n  `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\n  user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Methods marked **signed-in** below require a non-anonymous caller. Anonymous\n  callers receive a trap such as `Sign in to view your wallet`.\n- Registration prerequisite: a direct API caller must register before any\n  role-guarded call. Call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in\n  caller. The first principal to initialize becomes `#admin`; every subsequent\n  principal becomes `#user`. An unregistered caller that reaches a role-guarded\n  endpoint traps with `User is not registered` (from `getCallerUserRole`,\n  `isCallerAdmin`, and any admin-guarded method). Registration happens only when\n  a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never\n  did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a\n  signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal\n  than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Roles\n\n- `#admin` - full access, including catalog management and all-user views.\n- `#user` - standard signed-in access to wallet, purchases, and own history.\n- `#guest` - anonymous caller; role-guarded methods trap.\n\n`assignCallerUserRole(user, role)` lets an admin grant a role to another\nprincipal. Non-admins trap with\n`Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles`.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- All monetary amounts (`Amount`) are integer `Nat` values in the smallest\n  currency unit; there is no decimal point.\n- All timestamps (`Timestamp`) are `Nat` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch.\n- `UserId` is a `Principal`. `PhoneNumber` and `Reference` are `Text`.\n- `NetworkProvider` is `#mtn | #airtel | #glo | #nineMobile`.\n- `BillCategory` is `#electricity | #airtime | #cableTv | #internet`.\n- `OrderStatus` is `#pending | #completed | #failed`; orders and payments are\n  created directly as `#completed`.\n- `TransactionType` is `#topUp | #dataPurchase | #billPayment`.\n- Optional values (`?T`) are `null` when absent.\n\n## Wallet\n\n- `getMyWallet()` - **signed-in**. Returns the caller's `WalletView`\n  (`owner`, `balance`, `createdAt`). A caller with no wallet yet receives a\n  zero-balance view with `createdAt = 0`; the wallet record is created lazily on\n  the first credit or debit.\n- `getMyLedger()` - **signed-in**. Returns the caller's `LedgerEntry` list\n  (`id`, `owner`, `kind` `#credit|#debit`, `amount`, `reason`, `at`).\n- `topUpWallet(amount)` - **signed-in**. Credits the caller's wallet and returns\n  the created `LedgerEntry`. `amount` must be greater than zero, otherwise it\n  traps with `Top-up amount must be greater than zero`. Also records a `#topUp`\n  transaction with reference `TOPUP-<ledgerId>`.\n\n## Data reselling\n\n- `listDataBundles()` - public. Returns enabled `DataBundleView` records\n  (`id`, `provider`, `name`, `dataVolumeMb`, `validityDays`, `price`,\n  `enabled`). Disabled bundles are omitted.\n- `purchaseDataBundle(bundleId, recipient)` - **signed-in**. Debits the bundle\n  price from the caller's wallet and creates a completed `DataOrder`. Returns\n  `#ok(DataOrder)` or `#err(OrderError)`:\n  - `#notSignedIn` - anonymous caller.\n  - `#invalidInput` - empty `recipient`.\n  - `#notFound` - unknown or disabled bundle.\n  - `#insufficientFunds({ balance; required })` - wallet balance below price.\n  The order reference is `DATA-<orderId>`.\n\n## Bill payment\n\n- `listBillers()` - public. Returns enabled `BillerView` records\n  (`id`, `category`, `name`, `enabled`). Disabled billers are omitted.\n- `payBill(billerId, customerNumber, amount)` - **signed-in**. Debits `amount`\n  from the caller's wallet and creates a completed `BillPayment`. Returns\n  `#ok(BillPayment)` or `#err(OrderError)`:\n  - `#notSignedIn` - anonymous caller.\n  - `#invalidInput` - empty `customerNumber` or zero `amount`.\n  - `#notFound` - unknown or disabled biller.\n  - `#insufficientFunds({ balance; required })` - wallet balance below amount.\n  The payment reference is `BILL-<paymentId>`.\n\n## Transactions and history\n\n- `listTransactions(filter)` - **signed-in**. Returns the caller's transactions\n  matching `TransactionFilter` (`kind : ?TransactionType`, `from : ?Timestamp`,\n  `to : ?Timestamp`, `search : ?Text`). `from`/`to` are inclusive bounds on `at`.\n  `search` is a case-insensitive substring match against `reference` and\n  `counterparty`. A `null` field means no constraint.\n- `getTransaction(id)` - **signed-in**. Returns `?Transaction` for the caller's\n  own transaction, or `null` when it does not exist or belongs to another user.\n- `listMyDataOrders()` / `listMyBillPayments()` - **signed-in**. Return the\n  caller's own orders and payments.\n- `listAllDataOrders()` / `listAllBillPayments()` - **admin only**. Return every\n  user's orders and payments. Non-admins trap with\n  `Unauthorized: Only admins can view all orders` (or `... payments`).\n\n## Admin catalog management\n\nAll of the following are **admin only**; non-admins trap with\n`Unauthorized: Only admins can manage the catalog`.\n\n- `createDataBundle(provider, name, dataVolumeMb, validityDays, price)` -\n  creates an enabled bundle and returns its `DataBundleView`.\n- `updateDataBundle(id, provider, name, dataVolumeMb, validityDays, price, enabled)` -\n  returns `#ok(DataBundleView)` or `#err(#notFound)`.\n- `createBiller(category, name)` - creates an enabled biller and returns its\n  `BillerView`.\n- `updateBiller(id, category, name, enabled)` - returns `#ok(BillerView)` or\n  `#err(#notFound)`.\n\n## Lifecycle, retries, and gotchas\n\n- Purchases and payments are single-message operations: the wallet debit, the\n  order/payment record, and the transaction record are written together. A\n  successful call is final; there is no pending state to poll.\n- Retrying a purchase or payment creates a NEW order/payment and debits again.\n  There is no idempotency key, so do not retry a call that may have succeeded\n  without first checking `listMyDataOrders` / `listMyBillPayments` or the\n  transaction history.\n- `topUpWallet` is likewise not idempotent; each call credits again.\n- Wallet balance is derived from credits and debits; there is no external\n  payment rail - top-ups are applied directly.\n- Catalog reads (`listDataBundles`, `listBillers`) are public and safe to poll.\n- All other reads are `query` calls and safe to poll; they never mutate state.\n";
  };
};
